#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "0"
msgid "\nIn Hindu mythology, the golden armor and earrings worn by\nthe hero Karna. Karna's mother, Kunti, feared being an\nunmarried mother and prayed for the armor and earrings\nfrom Surya in order to protect her son.\n\nA powerful defensive Noble Phantasm that emits the radiance\nof the sun itself. Since it is light itself given shape,\neven a god would have difficulty destroying it,\nso Indra worked hard to circumvent it.\n\nIn the myth, Indra took the form of a Brahmin and visited\nKarna's castle. He approached Karna as he was bathing\nand said, \"Allow me to have the things you carry.\"\n\nKarna had sworn not to refuse the request of a Brahmin \nduring this time. While aware of Indra's trap, he accepted \nthe request and handed over what he had been asked: \nthe armor that was the only proof of his lineage.\n\n             ◆\n\nWhile taken from him in his myth, Karna still possesses it\nas a Servant. Seemingly weighty, it's an invincible armor\nthat protects against all manner of harmful interference,\nbe it physical or conceptual. \n\nSo long as he wears it, the damage Karna takes\nis reduced to one-tenth.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "1"
msgid "キーワード１偽名テキスト"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "2"
msgid "\nAccording to \"The Mahabharata,\" a feature that Karna\nwas well-known for was the generosity of a saint.\n\nThough Karna is poor at expressing his emotions,\nhe has the tendency to get angry when those who've\ncared for or supported him are scorned.\nEven if it's a relationship based only on give and take,\nKarna lives by repaying a favor with a favor.\n\nBecause of that selfless devotion of his, when people\ncame to him looking for something, he would generally\ngrant it to them, as long as they were being truthful.\n\nThis was because he would first consider the state\nof their heart before possessions or wealth they had.\n\n             ◆\n\nHowever, during the Holy Grail War, his master's victory\ntakes priority. To \"yield his victory\" would be refused,\nadmonishing his opponent for such an unwise proposal.\n\n\"What a ridiculous misunderstanding.\n In the first place, victory must be attained by oneself.\n Would a victory I hand you truly be a victory for you?\"\n\nThis is not out of sarcasm, but because the question of \n\"Wouldn't having victory handed to you be losing at life?\" \nis something he's actually worried about. \n\n"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "3"
msgid "キーワード２偽名テキスト"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "4"
msgid "\nA spear of light that only strikes once.\nA spear of mortality made of lightning.\n\nWhen the battle between Karna and Arjuna reached its\nfinal stages, in order to aid Arjuna, his father Indra,\nking of the gods, took Karna's greatest armor,\nhis \"Golden Armor\" through trickery.\n\nHowever, Karna's attitude at that time was so noble that\nIndra came to adore Karna, his son's enemy, and gave to him\nin compensation for taking his armor, the power of the\ngod of thunder that he never let anyone but himself wield.\n\nThis is that \"thunder spear.\"\nSaid to hold the power to defeat the gods themselves,\nthere is no record of Karna ever using it in his myth.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "5"
msgid "宝具偽名テキスト"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "6"
msgid "\nThe son of the sun god, Surya.\nSo he may later unify with Surya, he possess Divinity of\nthe highest rank. Against heroes related to sun gods with\nDivinity ranked B or lower, he manifests high defense.\n\n             ◆\n\nWhile Karna is poor at asserting himself, he displays\nfurious determination when it comes to protecting\nthe dignity of his father, the sun god.\n\nFor the motherless Karna, with his father the sun god as\nhis only certainty, and even receiving his power,\nhe swore to never do anything that would shame his father.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "7"
msgid "スキル１偽名テキスト"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "8"
msgid "\nWeapon mastery that went unrecognized for various reasons.\nSkills in sword, spear, bow, Riding, and Divinity are shown\nas down a rank, and attributes as their complete opposites.\nHowever, if his true name is known, the skill is dissolved.\n\nAlso, as a bit of an aside,\nthe rank of his luck stat was reported by Karna himself.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "9"
msgid "スキル２偽名テキスト"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "10"
msgid "\nThe ability to see through someone's personality\nand attributes. Cannot be deceived by words or excuses.\n\nHe was truly an incredibly thoughtful, superhuman hero.\nHe had the virtue to accept differing ideologies,\neven his enemy's, and respecting them as \"ways of living.\"\n\nBut Karna has difficulty conveying his true nature.\nHis attitude prods at others' true natures.\nActs to deceive oneself, behavior for show, beliefs.\nHe sees through it all and frankly states\n\"the true nature they want to hide.\"\n\nAs a result, he is disliked by most people he talks to\nand is forced into fights with them.\n\nAnyone would hate having their shortcomings revealed.\n\n             ◆\n\nNeedless to say, Karna's attitude does not come\nout of disgust for another('s faults).\n\nKarna affirms the standpoints of others, giving respect to\nbeliefs he doesn't share and values he can't understand.\nAs he can't put that admiration to words, he's misunderstood\nas someone who \"hates and denies everything.\"\n\n"
msgstr ""

